<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">20 July plot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Operation Valkyrie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 20 July plot was a failed attempt on 20 July 1944 to assassinate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> and overthrow the Nazi government, made by members of the German resistance, mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wehrmacht">Wehrmacht</a> officers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claus-von-stauffenberg">Claus von Stauffenberg</a> took a briefcase holding plastic explosive to a conference at the Wolf's Lair in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>; the blast killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enzo-of-sardinia">Heinz</a> Brandt and two others, but Hitler suffered only minor injuries. The coup attempt that followed, known as Operation Valkyrie, collapsed within hours, and Stauffenberg was executed by firing squad the same night. In the following months the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gestapo">Gestapo</a> arrested more than 7,000 people, 4,980 of whom were executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/20-july-plot.jpg" alt="20 July plot" width="330" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1972-025-10,_Hitler-Attentat,_20._Juli_1944.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
